<h2 align="center">Fledgling Quest </h2>
<p>Greetings One and All! </p>
<p>The point of having a Fledgling 
  Quest is to see if you are willing to do something to become a member of Random 
  Acts, to see how you relate to other members before you become a regular member, 
  and to demonstrate your willingness to help others. This last item is the foundation 
  of Random Acts--helping others is what we stand for.</p>
<h1>Overview: </h1>
<p>When a person first joins RA, they are a Fledgling Member. They must
have a regular member of RA sponsor them into the guild before they
become a fledgling member.</p>
<p>To become a Regular Member 
  of Random Acts, you must do the following: </p>
<ol>
  <li> Place a message on our Message Board within the Fledgling and
Prospective Member thread with your name and vital information and
explain why you wish to join us.</li>
  <li> Read <a href=candc.asp>The 
    Call and The Charter</a> on our webpage and see our message board. </li>
  <li> Seek out members of Random Acts, spend time getting to know them and
find a Sponsor among them.</li>
  <li> Your Sponsor will help you complete your Fledgling Quest and will
then recommend you for tagging. </li>
  <li> After you have been tagged for two weeks you will then be considered
a full regular member of Random Acts.</li>
</ol>
<p>You are encouraged to post 
  messages on the Message Board, attend our events, and get to know some of the 
  other members. In this way, You become a Regular Member through demonstrating 
  the willingness to practice (random or not random) acts of kindness while playing 
  EverQuest. </p>
<h1 align="center">Fledgling Quest </h1>
<p><b>Adopt-a-Newbie/Lowbie 
  Quest:</b> Assisting a newbie or lowbie (low level character) in game so that 
  they know the basics of EQ). </p>
<p>It is your task to find 
  a newbie, I mean a real newbie: someone who is new to EverQuest. (Or you can 
  find a lowbie if a newbie is not available) </p>
<p>Note: These newbies (or 
  lowbies) are not necessarily being brought into Random Acts as Fledglings. We 
  are just helping them learn EverQuest. </p>
<p>Then do some or all of the 
  following: </p>
<ol>
  <li> (Mandatory!) Get their 
    permission to help them. </li>
  <li> Tell them you will show 
    them the ways of Norrath (or your own phrasing) and all you ask in return 
    is that they remember your name and contact them in the future if they need 
    any more help. </li>
  <li> Teach them how to use 
    the Chat screen and the basic commands (e.g., /loc, /r, /t, etc.). </li>
  <li> Teach them how to hunt 
    if necessary. </li>
  <li> Teach them how to use 
    the Internet for information e.g., Allakhazam's, EQVault, EQAtlas, etc.) </li>
  <li> Make sure they know 
    the safe and unsafe places to go when traveling and hunting. </li>
  <li> Teach them the mail 
    quest (if of good race) and at least one other newbie quest. All together, 
    spend a minimum of three hours in real time helping them. </li>
</ol>
<p>When completed, you need 
  to send an e-mail to us at <a href="mailto:eqrandomacts@hotmail.com">eqrandomacts@hotmail.com</a>. 
  You do NOT need to have your newbie/lowbie contact us--we take your word for 
  it. </p>
<p>Recommended but not required: 
  </p>
<ul>
  <li> Keep their name and 
    check back with them once in a while over the next couple of weeks to see 
    if they need any more help and to answer their questions. </li>
  <li> Giving them items is 
    not required nor is it forbidden, but Random Acts does not want to encourage 
    players begging for items. </li>
</ul>
<h1 align="center">Community 
  Service </h1>
<p><b>Serving-the-Guild Quest</b>: 
  Assisting a Council Member (or a Regular Member) with a guild task. For this 
  option you need a Council Member's approval. </p>
<p>In this Quest you would 
  contact the Council and see if any one of the Council Members has anything that 
  you can assist with. If you have a specific idea, please let us know. </p>
<p>Good Luck! </p>
